<article class="eden-editorial page container">
  <header class="rooms-header text-center">
    <span class="hero-eyebrow">Desire Riviera Maya</span>
    <h1>The Eden Guide</h1>
    <p class="hero-lead" style="max-width: var(--max-paragraph); margin: 0 auto 28px; color: var(--color-espresso-soft);">
      Eden is a distinct accommodation section within Desire Riviera Maya. The easiest way to understand it is as a different room-and-service tier within the same resort, not a separate resort.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="verdict-banner text-center" style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto 42px;">
    <h2>What Eden Actually Changes</h2>
    <p>
      Desire describes Eden as an exclusive section with more lavish accommodations, enhanced privacy, and elevated VIP amenities. At the same time, Eden guests retain access to the wider Riviera Maya resort, including its restaurants, bars, beach, clothing-optional areas, and spa. The practical question is therefore not whether Eden replaces the main resort, but whether the additional room features and service matter enough for your stay.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="room-difference-guide" aria-labelledby="eden-decision-heading">
    <div class="room-difference-guide__intro">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Before You Book</span>
      <h2 id="eden-decision-heading">Four Things to Compare</h2>
      <p>Current Eden categories differ mainly by <strong>view</strong>, <strong>private water feature</strong>, <strong>suite tier</strong>, and <strong>service level</strong>. Start with the feature you will actually use rather than assuming the highest-priced category is automatically the best fit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="room-difference-guide__grid">
      <div class="room-difference-guide__item"><strong>View</strong><span>Choose among tropical/garden, main-pool, and ocean-view settings depending on which outlook matters to you.</span></div>
      <div class="room-difference-guide__item"><strong>Jacuzzi</strong><span>Several Eden suites have an indoor jacuzzi. The current Diamond Jacuzzi category adds a larger suite layout and ocean view.</span></div>
      <div class="room-difference-guide__item"><strong>Swim-up</strong><span>Beloved, Seductive, and Diamond each have a current swim-up option. These are different from suites whose defining private water feature is an indoor jacuzzi.</span></div>
      <div class="room-difference-guide__item"><strong>Service</strong><span>Current Eden categories list services such as butler service, airport transfer, room breakfast, VIP check-in, premium bars, or other extras depending on category.</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="room-difference-guide__note">Room names, features, services, rates, and availability can change. Confirm the exact category and current inclusions when you book.</p>
  </section>

